## 9. API Error Handling

| HTTP status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `400 Bad Request` | Invalid URL, alias or expiration value |
| `401 Unauthorized` | Authentication is required |
| `403 Forbidden` | Unsafe, blocked or unauthorized destination |
| `404 Not Found` | Short code is missing, expired or inactive |
| `409 Conflict` | Custom alias already exists |
| `429 Too Many Requests` | Rate limit or quota exceeded |
| `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server failure |
| `503 Service Unavailable` | Required component is temporarily unavailable |

Errors should help API consumers understand the problem without exposing sensitive internal details.

