## 10. HTTP 301 vs 302 Redirect

### 10.1 301 Permanent Redirect

Advantages:

- Browsers may cache the redirect.
- Repeat visits may not reach the shortener.
- Origin traffic is reduced.
- Repeat redirects may be faster.

Disadvantages:

- Repeat clicks may bypass analytics.
- Analytics becomes incomplete.
- Changing the destination becomes difficult.
- Disabling a malicious link may not take effect immediately.

### 10.2 302 Temporary Redirect

Advantages:

- Clicks continue passing through the shortener.
- Analytics remains more accurate.
- The destination can be updated.
- Expiration can be enforced.
- Malicious URLs can be disabled.

Disadvantages:

- More requests reach the URL shortener.
- Infrastructure load is higher.

### Decision

Use `302` when analytics, expiration and destination control are important.

Use `301` only when the destination is permanent and complete analytics is not required.

