## 14. Main URL Mapping Schema

Primary access pattern:

> Find the long URL using the short code.

Logical schema:

~~~text
URLMapping
----------
short_code
long_url
user_id
created_at
expires_at
is_custom
is_active
status
metadata
~~~

Primary key:

> short_code

Example record:

~~~json
{
  "short_code": "abc123",
  "long_url": "https://example.com/products/123",
  "user_id": "user-1001",
  "created_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
  "expires_at": "2027-11-23T10:00:00Z",
  "is_custom": false,
  "is_active": true,
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}
~~~

Do not update this record on every click.

A popular link could create:

- Write contention
- Hot partitions
- Increased redirect latency
- Database write pressure

Click events should be processed separately.

