## 32. Rate Limiting

Rate limiting protects against:

- Bot traffic
- URL creation spam
- Namespace exhaustion
- Malicious campaigns
- Unexpected infrastructure cost
- API abuse

Example quotas:

| User type | Limit |
|---|---|
| Anonymous | 10 shortenings per hour per IP |
| Registered | 100 shortenings per hour |
| Premium | 10,000 shortenings per hour |

Possible algorithms:

- Token bucket
- Leaky bucket
- Fixed window
- Sliding window log
- Sliding window counter

Rate-limit using:

- IP address
- User ID
- API key
- Account
- Destination domain

Response:

~~~http
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 3600
~~~

A distributed rate limiter may use Redis atomic operations or scripts.

