## 40. Important Trade-Offs

### 301 vs 302

~~~text
301:
Better browser caching
Lower origin traffic
Weaker analytics and control

302:
Better analytics and control
Higher infrastructure traffic
~~~

### Hashing vs Counter

~~~text
Hashing:
Simple generation
Truncated output can collide

Counter:
Guaranteed uniqueness
Counter must be scaled
~~~

### SQL vs NoSQL

~~~text
SQL:
Strong constraints
Rich queries
Relationships

NoSQL:
Horizontal scalability
Fast key-value lookup
High throughput
~~~

### Synchronous vs Asynchronous Analytics

~~~text
Synchronous:
Immediate analytics
Slower redirect

Asynchronous:
Fast redirect
Eventually consistent analytics
~~~

### Deduplication vs Separate Short URLs

~~~text
Deduplication:
Less storage
Same code for the same URL

Separate short URLs:
More storage
Separate analytics for every campaign
~~~

### Global Writes vs Primary-Region Writes

~~~text
Global writes:
Lower regional latency
Higher conflict complexity

Primary-region writes:
Simpler uniqueness
Higher latency for distant users
~~~

### CDN Caching vs Complete Analytics

~~~text
More CDN caching:
Lower latency
Lower origin load
Potentially less origin-level analytics

Less CDN caching:
More complete origin visibility
Higher infrastructure load
~~~

