## 41. Common Anti-Patterns

Avoid:

- Processing heavy analytics inside the redirect request.
- Updating the main URL row on every click.
- Using `301` while promising complete analytics.
- Using truncated hashes without collision handling.
- Depending on one global counter without a scaling plan.
- Ignoring custom alias race conditions.
- Skipping URL validation.
- Allowing unlimited URL creation.
- Hitting the database on every redirect.
- Storing raw analytics forever.
- Allowing analytics failure to stop redirects.
- Ignoring viral hot keys.
- Caching a redirect beyond its expiration time.
- Treating obfuscated URLs as private URLs.
- Making the creation service a dependency of the redirect service.

