## 48. Top 10 Points to Remember

1. A URL shortener is a read-heavy system.
2. Redirect latency is more important than URL creation latency.
3. The short-code lookup is the core hot path.
4. Use `302` when analytics and destination control matter.
5. Truncated hashes can create collisions.
6. Counter-based or distributed IDs with Base62 provide reliable uniqueness.
7. Custom aliases require atomic conflict handling.
8. Caching prevents every redirect from reaching the database.
9. Analytics should be asynchronous and eventually consistent.
10. Viral links create hot-key and hot-partition problems.

